     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div>I&#39;ve been looking around on the users group and on the wiki but can&#39;t find any information on this issue. Apologies if it has been raised before.</div><div><br><div>I&#39;ve found a weird quirk when examining the results of an integrated fisheries model built in TMB. If I return values from the TMB model using REPORT() as well as ADREPORT() the values differ by a very small percentage. In most instances this is very inconsequential but when returning estimates of large numbers such as absolute biomass the differences can become important. I also noticed that these differences get larger as the model timestep increases. Here is the printout of the same quantity from the TMB model using ADREPORT vs REPORT along with the differences: </div><div><br></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">     Year      ADREPORT    REPORT    difference<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">1  1992</span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">     </span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"> 693137.3 </span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">   </span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">693137.3 \r\n-0.002377396</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">2  1993</span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">     </span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"> 655004.1 </span><span style=\"font-size:11p